{"node":{"id":"HP:0002074","label":"Increased neuronal autofluorescent lipopigment","ic":7.16,"definition":"Lipofuscin, a generic term applied to autofluorescent lipopigment, is a mixture of protein and lipid that accumulates in most aging cells, particularly those involved in high lipid turnover (e.g., the adrenal medulla) or phagocytosis of other cell types (e g., the retinal pigment epithelium or RPE; macrophage). This term pertains if there is an increase in the neuronal accumulation of lipofuscin (also known as autofluorescent lipoprotein) more than expected for the age of the patient."},"diseases":[{"id":"MONDO:0008083","label":"ceroid lipofuscinosis, neuronal, 4 (Kufs type)","in_core":true,"edge":{"id":"e_cb4abe89972e","source":"MONDO:0008083","target":"HP:0002074","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":"OMIM:162350 · OMIM:162350","url":"https://omim.org/entry/162350","level":"curated","date":"2009-02-17","confidence":0.5,"snippet":"Ceroid lipofuscinosis, neuronal, 4B, autosomal dominant: Increased neuronal autofluorescent lipopigment [IEA]"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":0.5,"independent_sources":["OMIM"],"level":"curated"},"confidence":0.5},{"id":"MONDO:0008767","label":"neuronal ceroid lipofuscinosis 3","in_core":true,"edge":{"id":"e_579140f248bd","source":"MONDO:0008767","target":"HP:0002074","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":"OMIM:204200 · OMIM:204200","url":"https://omim.org/entry/204200","level":"curated","date":"2009-02-17","confidence":0.5,"snippet":"Ceroid lipofuscinosis, neuronal, 3: Increased neuronal autofluorescent lipopigment [IEA]"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":0.5,"independent_sources":["OMIM"],"level":"curated"},"confidence":0.5},{"id":"MONDO:0008768","label":"ceroid lipofuscinosis, neuronal, 6B (Kufs type)","in_core":true,"edge":{"id":"e_942d7324317a","source":"MONDO:0008768","target":"HP:0002074","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","rec